{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dot product dot product","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md","fileName":"Dot Product.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dot Product","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-16 23:45\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Cartesian Analytic Geometry]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cartesian Analytic Geometry","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf","foundationsofmath.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dot product dot product","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md","fileName":"Dot Product.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dot Product","heading":"Dot Product","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For planar vectors $u=(u_1,u_2)$ and $v=(v_1,v_2)$, the dot product is $u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2$. The result is a scalar. It also satisfies $u\\cdot v=\\|u\\|\\|v\\|\\cos\\theta$, so a zero dot product identifies perpendicular nonzero vectors and the sign records whether their angle is acute or obtuse.\n\nWith normalized vectors, a game can use the dot product directly as the cosine of the angle between directions. The sign quickly distinguishes whether a target is generally in front of, beside, or behind an object's facing direction.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cartesian Analytic Geometry","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf","foundationsofmath.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"dot product dot product","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Dot Product.md","fileName":"Dot Product.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Dot Product","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf]]\n[[foundationsofmath.pdf]]\n[[gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Cartesian Analytic Geometry","gameprogrammingincplusplus.pdf","foundationsofmath.pdf","gameprogrammingalgorithmsandtechniques.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}